Let Keystone log JSON.

This is the first service to honour openstack_logging_json, and the one
that proves the mechanism end to end: every job deploys Keystone, so
any scenario that sets the option exercises the Fluentd JSON path
added in the previous patch.

The option is referenced directly rather than through a
keystone_logging_json indirection, which is how keystone_logging_debug
works. Debug can sensibly differ per service. The log format cannot:
every oslo.log service is tailed by the single input in
conf/input/00-global.conf.j2, that input has one parser, and a service
logging a different format to its neighbours would not be parsed at
all. Making it look per service would offer a setting that quietly
breaks log collection.

Prompt: Michael asked how much work it would be to let every oslo.log
service in Kolla-Ansible log JSON using the parser added for Kerbside,
and asked for the structural changes and one demonstration conversion
to land in small patches ahead of the bulk conversion. This is the
demonstration.

